  "reason": "The prediction states that bodily and emotional feelings survive bilateral destruction of the insula, while flattening or abolition of feelings counts against it. In this study, bilateral insular lesions in rats significantly weakened alcohol-induced taste aversion, completely blocked alcohol-induced place aversion, and eliminated a neophobic-like response. Using the authors' framing of conditioned responses as a proxy for perceived subjective interoceptive properties, these lesions flattened or abolished the negative feelings studied.",
